Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (Exchange record, Tee; AC9, AC10, AC11, AC12)
Why this approach: each test goes through run and a real store and asserts on the reader's row after a stop that drains the queue, with checkNoCaptureLeaks after every stop. A new bodyUpstream keeps the request body upstream read, so the stored request is compared with what reached upstream and not only with what the client sent. The AC11 test caps both directions at 1000 bytes and writes the response in 333-byte pieces, so the cap falls inside a write.
Alternatives rejected: changing core so a refused dial does not set request_incomplete. The spec defines the flag as the copy sealed before the client's body reached its end, and on a refused dial the transport never reads the body. So gateway_502 asserts request_incomplete together with gateway_error and no stored request body (recorded in plan.md, "Details fixed in T17"). Also rejected: bounding ended_at by the client's clock. The handler can return after the client has read the whole body, which was seen once as a flake, so only started_at is bounded.
Trade-off / known limit: no code fix was needed; the guard found only the two behaviours above, and both are recorded rather than changed. AC11's non_streamed_json_parses_partial subtest needs the parser and is left to its later task. request_read_after_seal sends a 32 MiB body so that loopback's socket buffers can't absorb it.
Verified by: make verify; go test -race -count=5 on TestCapture_ExchangeStored (streamed, non_streamed), TestCapture_EncodedBodyStoredAsSent, TestCapture_BodyOverCapTruncated, TestCapture_AbortedExchangesRecorded (client_disconnect, upstream_abort, gateway_502, request_read_after_seal). Mutations, each reverted: HasTTFB false and unredacted request headers each failed ExchangeStored; dropping Content-Encoding from the response snapshot failed EncodedBodyStoredAsSent; the response copy skipping its first byte failed ExchangeStored and EncodedBodyStoredAsSent; a cap one byte over failed BodyOverCapTruncated; zeroing ClientDisconnected, UpstreamAborted, RequestIncomplete and GatewayError in finishCapture failed each AbortedExchangesRecorded subtest on its own flag.
